    "<table class=\"tbl\">\n         <tr><th>equation</th><th>when it has a solution</th><th>all solutions ($k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$)</th></tr>\n         <tr><td>$\\sin x = a$</td><td>$|a| \\le 1$</td><td>$x = x_0 + 2k\\pi$ or $x = \\pi - x_0 + 2k\\pi$</td></tr>\n         <tr><td>$\\cos x = a$</td><td>$|a| \\le 1$</td><td>$x = \\pm x_0 + 2k\\pi$</td></tr>\n         <tr><td>$\\mathrm{tg}\\,x = a$</td><td>always</td><td>$x = x_0 + k\\pi$</td></tr>\n       </table>\n       <p>Here $x_0$ is one root (e.g. the reference angle with a suitable sign). Equations with sine and cosine have no solution when $|a| &gt; 1$.</p>",
    "<p><strong>Substitution.</strong> We solve the equation $2\\sin^2 x - \\sin x - 1 = 0$ as a quadratic equation in the unknown $t = \\sin x$: $2t^2 - t - 1 = 0$ has the roots $t_1 = 1$, $t_2 = -\\frac{1}{2}$. Then we solve $\\sin x = 1$ and $\\sin x = -\\frac{1}{2}$ separately.</p>"
